+# SMS verification integration
+
+The homepage supplies the accessible phone/code forms, purpose selection, native
+one-time-code autofill, progressive WebOTP extraction, and send/resend/verify
+request handling. This repository is static: it does not contain an SMS provider
+or authentication service. No code is accepted and no session is established in
+the client. Until the following endpoints exist, requests display an availability
+error rather than pretending to send a text or sign a customer in.
+
+## Same-origin API contract
+
+Both endpoints accept POST requests with JSON, return JSON, and must be served
+alongside this page over HTTPS. The HTML actions match these endpoints; if native
+(non-JavaScript) submission is supported, also accept form-encoded requests and
+render the appropriate next step.
+
+- `POST /api/auth/sms/request`: `{ "phone": "+15551234567", "purpose": "rewards" }`
+  (`purpose` is `rewards` or `order`). Return
+  `{ "challengeId": "opaque-server-challenge-id" }` only after the provider accepts
+  the SMS request. A resend creates a new challenge and invalidates the old code.
+- `POST /api/auth/sms/verify`: `{ "challengeId": "…", "phone": "+15551234567",
+  "purpose": "rewards", "code": "012345" }`. Verify the challenge server-side,
+  establish the authenticated session with a Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite cookie,
+  then return `{ "verified": true }`. The client advances to `/rewards` or
+  `/order-online`; those destinations must enforce authentication themselves.
+- Use non-2xx responses for failures, including 400/401/410 for invalid or expired
+  codes and 429 with a numeric `Retry-After` header for rate limits. Do not include
+  sensitive account-existence information in errors. The UI never displays raw
+  server error text.
+
+Generate codes securely and preserve leading zeros. Bind challenges to phone,
+purpose, and the requesting session; expire them, limit attempts and resends,
+consume them once, and validate every request on the server. Enforce same-origin
+requests/CSRF protection and server-side rate limits; the client’s 30-second resend
+countdown is a convenience, not a security boundary. Never log plaintext codes.
+
+## SMS format
+
+Use the actual host serving the page on the **last line**, with no scheme, port,
+path, or trailing signature. For example, when hosted at `dailygrind.example`:
+
+```text
+Your Daily Grind verification code is 012345.
+
+@dailygrind.example #012345
+```
+
+WebOTP is feature-detected in secure contexts and starts before the send request.
+The listener is cancelled on resend, phone/purpose changes, submission, timeout,
+and page exit. A received code uses the same validated submit handler. Browsers
+without WebOTP retain OS autofill via `autocomplete="one-time-code"`, paste, and
+manual input in one labeled field. The form does not request access to a message
+inbox or require an SMS-reading polyfill.
